2026-10-20 04:07 Implemented: verify_token fetches the keys again only when Crypt::JWT reports 'kid_keys lookup failed'; every other rejection is thrown unchanged and costs no request. New attribute jwks_min_age (is => ro, default 60) with POD, private attribute _jwks_fetched. Decision (coordinator rule left room here): _jwks_fetched records the last *forced* fetch, so the first cached fetch does not start the rate-limit window - otherwise a fresh process could not refresh at all in its first 60s and the card's 'unknown kid causes exactly one JWKS GET' would never hold. Tests (t/02-oidc.t, t/04-oidc-verify-alg.t) were red against the old lib (6 + 1 failures, all behavioural), green after the fix. Suite: 422 tests green. Commit a7282f6.

